  "question": "Let $A, B$ be $3 \\times 3$ matrices such that $|A| = 2$ and $|B| = -3$. What is $|2A^{-1}B|$?",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "$|2A^{-1}B| = |2A^{-1}|\\times|B|$<br />$|2A^{-1}| = 2^3|A^{-1}| = 8\\times|A^{-1}|$<br />$|A^{-1}| = \\frac{1}{|A|} = \\frac{1}{2}$<br />$\\Rightarrow |2A^{-1}| = 8\\times \\frac{1}{2} = 4$<br /><br />Now, $|2A^{-1}B| = 4 \\times (-3) = -12$.<br />Answer: (A) $-12$.",
